    "title": "Comcast customers: Here’s how to get your part of $117.5M data breach settlement",
    "text": "NewsComcast has agreed to a $117.5 million data breach settlement. Comcast via AP ImagesBy Karin Price Mueller | NJ.comIf you were a Comcast customer in 2023, you could be eligible for part of a $117.5 million data breach settlement. The settlement ends a class action lawsuit that alleged the company failed to properly protect personal information of customers. The lawsuit was filed after Comcast, in December 2023, announced hackers accessed the personal information of millions of Xfinity customers between Oct. 16, 2023 and Oct. 19, 2023.Comcast denied any wrongdoing, according to the settlement website. It did not immediately respond to requests for comment. Eligible consumers should have received a notification about the data breach, but if you didn’t — or you don’t remember — you can look up your status on the settlement website at comcastbreachsettlement.com.The amount each customer will receive will depend on several factors including how many claims are filed, but if you had to spend money or time to deal with fraud or identity theft, you may be reimbursed your losses, the website said. “As an alternative to making a claim for Out-of-Pocket Losses and Lost Time, Settlement Class Members may request an Alternative Cash Payment, estimated in the amount of $50 subject to pro rata adjustment,” the website said. Eligible customers are also entitled to three years of credit monitoring services, it said. You must submit a valid claim form by Aug. 14, it said.Cancer cluster fears dominate packed town meeting. ‘It’s a big freaking deal.’ Feared N.J. cancer cluster update: Town slams state after bombshell report‘Ridiculous.’ Why Trump official’s advice to put more money in your pocket could backfire.",
